    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When the hot weather pushed demand higher in May, it left little room for error on the power grid. The broken generator everyone relied on—Unit 2—went offline unexpectedly, adding to the crunch. After a wave of generator failures hit since the month began, the system went on high alert, forcing officials to make the tough call of emergency load shedding to protect the grid. The result was a huge chunk of power lost, over 950 megawatts, leaving ordinary households and businesses facing the threat of rolling blackouts in the Visayas region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-2",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The persistent outages that were never fixed, combined with high demand from the heatwave, strained the grid. Infrastructure managers had to issue a red alert for the island region when equipment malfunctions multiplied. People's power was shut off to protect the transmission lines, but the generation shortfall—over 950 megawatts—meant the risk of blackouts grew, hitting everyday communities hardest.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A key power plant broke down, and with many generators already failing, the authorities had to step in. The grid operator warned everyone of a power system emergency, leading to a decision to cut electricity to prevent a larger collapse. This equipment failure left a massive power capacity loss, and people in the affected area now faced the real danger of losing power in turns—a direct hit to their daily lives and livelihoods.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
